      "knowledge_point_id": "be11193b-a241-5812-a1c1-54d233ae9ddd",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining the Value of a Binomial Coefficient",
      "problem": "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $(\\frac{2}{1}).$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the value of $(\\frac{2}{1}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $2$ and position $1$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe value located in row $2$ and position $1$ is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  & 1 &  & 2 &  & 1 \\\\  &  & 1 &  & 3 &  & 3 &  & 1 \\\\  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(\\frac{2}{1})=2.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
