      "math_academy_id": "q-70311",
      "knowledge_point_id": "e5c108c0-f32a-5725-af3b-c3e747da09f2",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating Binomial Coefficients Using the Formula",
      "problem": "Determine the value of $(\\frac{7}{3}).$",
      "worked_solution": "The binomial coefficient $(\\frac{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\frac{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=7$ and $r=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{7}{3}) & =\\frac{7!}{(7-3)!\\cdot 3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4!}{4!\\cdot 3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot \\cancel{6}\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{\\cancel{4!}\\cdot \\cancel{6}} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
