      "worked_solution": "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=7$ and $r=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{5}) & =\\frac{7!}{(7-5)!\\cdot 5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5!}{2!\\cdot 5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{2\\cdot \\cancel{5!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{42}{2} \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
