      "knowledge_point": "Calculating Binomial Coefficients Using the Formula",
      "problem": "Determine the value of $(\\frac{8}{5}).$",
      "worked_solution": "The binomial coefficient $(\\frac{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\frac{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=8$ and $r=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{8}{5}) & =\\frac{8!}{(8-5)!\\cdot 5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5!}{3!\\cdot 5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5!}{6\\cdot 5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot \\cancel{6}\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{6}\\cdot \\cancel{5!}} \\\\  & =8\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
