      "math_academy_id": "e-5108",
      "knowledge_point_id": "be11193b-a241-5812-a1c1-54d233ae9ddd",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining the Value of a Binomial Coefficient",
      "problem": "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $\\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the value of $\\displaystyle{\\color{red}{3} \\choose {\\color{blue}2}},$ we need to find the number that is located in row $\\color{red}3$ and position $\\color{blue}2$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important:** Remember that when counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero!\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe value located in row $\\color{red}3$ and position $\\color{blue}2$ is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  & 1 &  & 1 \\\\  &  & 1 &  & 2 &  & 1 \\\\  & 1 &  & 3 &  & 3 &  & 1 \\\\ ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2} = 3.$",
      "difficulty": null,
      "answer_fields": [],
      "missing_source_fields": [
        "difficulty",
        "answer_fields"
      ]
    },
    {
      "math_academy_id": "e-5109",
      "knowledge_point_id": "9c976b6a-4523-51e1-a243-27aa8937db25",
      "knowledge_point": "Expressing the Relationship Between the Rows of Pascal's Triangle in Terms of Binomial Coefficients",
      "problem": "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3} = \\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2} + \\displaystyle{\\left[ \\phantom{3 \\choose 3}\\right]}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "To find $\\displaystyle{\\color{red}{4} \\choose {\\color{blue}3}},$ we need to find the number that is located in row $\\color{red}4$ and position $\\color{blue}3$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important:** Remember that when counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero!\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3}$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\frac{3}{0}) &  & (\\frac{3}{1}) &  & (\\frac{3}{2}) &  & (\\frac{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\frac{4}{0}) &  & (\\frac{4}{1}) &  & (\\frac{4}{2}) &  & (\\frac{4}{3}) &  & (\\frac{4}{4}) \\\\  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3}$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3} = \\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2} + \\displaystyle{3 \\choose 3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\displaystyle{3 \\choose 3}.$",
